        "Open Data": "",
        "Anomalies?": "",
        "Notes": "The Hyper-Kamiokande (Hyper-K) detector is a next generation underground water Cherenkov detector, about 25 times larger than Super-Kamiokande. It is a multipurpose detector but it will be mainly the far detector of a future long baseline neutrino experiment, envisioned for the upgraded J-PARC beam. Hyper-Kamiokande is also able to study proton decays, atmospheric neutrinos, and neutrinos from astro-physical origins. It is currently under construction and will begin running in 2027.",
